const healthText = `Read the school notice and Leo's message.

Health Week: If you feel unwell during the school day, tell a teacher or the school nurse. Do not share bottles or cups. Cover your mouth and nose when you cough or sneeze, then wash your hands. The school nurse can help you decide whom to contact; she does not give medicine without a parent's permission.

On Tuesday, Leo told his teacher that he had a headache and felt hot. His teacher called his father, who picked him up and arranged for him to get advice from a health professional. Leo stayed home while he felt unwell. His classmates cleaned shared desk surfaces and made a get-well card. On Thursday, Leo's father said Leo felt better and would return when he was ready. Leo thanked the class but reminded them that a card was kind; it could not replace proper care.`

const cultureText = `Read the welcome-day report.

At a school welcome afternoon, exchange student Ana helped make a small greeting guide. Her partner Ken said that his family usually waved to guests, while his cousin often bowed. At the welcome table, visitors could wave, say hello, or shake hands if both people felt comfortable. The group wrote that there was no single greeting for every person in a country. Before taking a photo, students should ask the person for permission. When Ana saw a snack with no label, she asked a teacher to check its ingredients instead of guessing. The students learned that customs can differ among families and that a polite question is better than a quick judgment.`

const volunteerText = `Read the report and the signup notice.

At Riverside Community Library, teen volunteers run a Saturday Book Corner. A volunteer helps a younger reader choose a book, reads with the child for 15 minutes, and then returns the book to the correct shelf. Volunteers work in pairs. They do not collect money or take children outside the library. Last month, 12 volunteers helped at four sessions. The sign-in sheet recorded 31 child-visits because some children came more than once; the library did not count the number of different children.

Next month's signup notice: Four Saturday sessions | 9:00–10:30 a.m. | Book Room | Grades 8–9 | Sign up by Wednesday, 4:00 p.m. | Six volunteers at most per session | Contact: Ms. Lee | Books are provided.`

